<p>Iran said it is ready to let Japanese vessels pass through the Strait of Hormuz and help them do so. In a phone interview with Kyodo News, Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said talks with Tokyo are under way and that the waterway remains open. Araghchi delivered the message directly to Japanese media as Tehran and Tokyo discuss continued access to the route.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VHtWBCmQW1LJaTZckaO7UtJEUFMQpuopNmG7FeymmvngJGuwZ6exXlijzFRj6sCkKXwvuOzyhigOUhp3sey6n4dGNi7Rsg6mGGP4_wN7CN8pjeOCDf-B_HiKdXdSyFaC9QQLLwlddv6NdRn-dOY8vtb3YrkJP1oTLNjuPHH-1F2fwL0gImm4YNRh' alt='The Strait of Hormuz, a key route for global energy shipments' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Conditional passage: Iran framed the offer as safe passage it can help arrange for countries like Japan if they coordinate directly with Tehran, pointing to a managed-transit approach rather than an unrestricted blanket guarantee.</li><li>Energy exposure: The announcement matters especially for Japan because about 90% of its crude imports come from the Middle East, making any disruption around Hormuz especially consequential for the country.</li><li>Conflict backdrop: In the same interview, Araghchi tied the situation to late-February attacks by the United States and Israel and said Iran was seeking “not a ceasefire, but a complete” end to the conflict.</li></ul><blockquote>We have not closed the strait. It is open. - Abbas Araghchi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian government: Araghchi said Tehran has already opened talks with Tokyo on the passage issue, presenting it as an active bilateral discussion rather than a sudden unilateral move. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-ready-to-let-japanese-vessels-transit-strait-of-hormuz-say-reports/article70768281.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Japan: Tokyo&#x27;s immediate concern is keeping tanker traffic moving, since Japanese energy buyers remain heavily reliant on Middle East crude shipped through Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/21/iran-says-it-will-allow-japanese-ships-to-transit-the-strait-of-hormuz'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Iranian diplomacy: Tehran said any assistance would depend on direct coordination, signaling that it wants a hands-on role in managing safe transit for ships from countries like Japan. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-ready-to-help-passage-of-japan-ships-in-strait-of-hormuz-says-foreign-minister'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-ready-to-let-japanese-vessels-transit-strait-of-hormuz-say-reports/article70768281.ece'>Iran ready to let Japanese vessels transit Strait of Hormuz, say reports</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/21/iran-says-it-will-allow-japanese-ships-to-transit-the-strait-of-hormuz'>Iran says it will allow Japanese ships to transit the Strait of Hormuz</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-ready-to-help-passage-of-japan-ships-in-strait-of-hormuz-says-foreign-minister'>Iran ready to help passage of Japan ships in Strait of Hormuz, says foreign minister</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3347415/iran-ready-help-japan-ships-pass-through-strait-hormuz-araghchi-says'>Iran ready to help Japan ships pass through Strait of Hormuz, Araghchi says</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c36rny6xgppo'>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi says that Iran is ready to help the passage of vessels from Japan in the Strait of Hormuz.</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>